# pagination.zd — one page of a long list at a time.
#
# `page` is the caller's `Whole` signal, counted from zero because
# `indices` and `listTake`/`listDrop` are; the numbers a reader sees are
# `page + 1`, converted in one place here rather than at every use site.
#
# THE DECISION WORTH NAMING: there is no disabled Previous.
#
# A pagination bar on the first page normally shows a greyed-out Previous,
# and the vocabulary cannot express one — the closed argument set has no
# `disabled` attribute, only a `disabled` *style prefix* for colouring a
# control that is disabled by some other means. Rather than emit a live
# button that silently does nothing on the first page, this renders no
# button there at all. A control that is absent is honest; a control that
# is present and inert is the failure the attribute exists to prevent, and
# it is worse for a keyboard user than for anybody else, because it is a
# tab stop that leads nowhere.
#
# WHAT IS MISSING: `aria-current="page"` on the current number. As in
# `breadcrumbs.zd`, it is hyphenated and therefore unspellable, so the
# current page is distinguished by being the one entry that is not a
# button — visible to everyone, announced to nobody.

component Pagination with page, count, class, pageClass, currentClass
    Navigation class is class, title is "Pagination"
        Row
            if page > 0
                Button "Previous", class is pageClass
                    on click
                        subtract 1 from page
            each index in (indices of count)
                PageNumber index, page is page, pageClass is pageClass, currentClass is currentClass
            if page < count - 1
                Button "Next", class is pageClass
                    on click
                        add 1 to page

component PageNumber with index, page, pageClass, currentClass
    if index is page
        Text (index + 1), class is currentClass
    otherwise
        Button (index + 1), class is pageClass
            on click
                set page to index
